The legal texts are royal decrees and laws of the Sultanate of Oman, as published in the Official Gazette
(الجريدة الرسمية). They were read from:

  Qanoon.om (https://qanoon.om), which transcribes the Official Gazette, retrieved 29 October 2026. Qanoon.om states:
  "نصوص القانون تعد ملكا عاما في سلطنة عمان بموجب أحكام قانون حق المؤلف والحقوق المجاورة العماني ويجوز لمستخدمي موقع
  Qanoon.om استعمالها ونسخها ونشرها وترجمتها مجانا ودون قيود" (the texts of law are public property in Oman under the
  Omani Copyright and Related Rights Law and may be used, copied, published and translated freely and without
  restriction). It also states that it is not an official source.

and checked against the Ministry of Justice and Legal Affairs (وزارة العدل والشؤون القانونية, https://mjla.gov.om),
whose content is licensed under the Government Open Licence - Sultanate of Oman (الرخصة الحكومية المفتوحة - سلطنة عمان).

Changes made by Lexifina: each text was converted to one Markdown file per article, one paragraph per line; spacing,
quotes, dashes and digit forms were normalised; the site's footnotes were removed from the text and used only to credit
the amending decree; and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the decrees that made each change. The
wording of the law was not changed. Neither Qanoon.om nor the Ministry endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
